From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alfred Ben <e0958604@u.nus.edu>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:24:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] index, explore: cut the resident footprint of the word
 index

The first ranked search after load or after an edit rebuilt the word
index and the call graph on malloc, and macOS malloc keeps large freed
chunks dirty. Compaction also dropped contents that were zero-copy
slices of the snapshot mmap, which forced disk reads.

- overlay edits on the mmap word index and map the index after persist
- rebuild the word index once, in a private malloc zone
- keep snapshot-mapped contents; compaction frees only heap contents
- unmap the call-graph arena (page_allocator)
- keep zero-token docs on adoption and cap overlay prefix work

Warm start on a 16k-file repo: 547 MiB -> 168-185 MiB phys_footprint.
